  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342273",
      "title": "Should You Switch From Node to Deno?",
      "lectureOrder": 531,
      "videoOrder": 471,
      "sourceHash": "bb5f1d3d3a0257880140f969f75a0082277ed2b8d3d53d54789a30a410885fa1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.24,
          "end": 4.68,
          "en": "So it's time for a comparison,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.68,
          "end": 6.211,
          "en": "which one is better?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.211,
          "end": 10.414,
          "en": "Well, as you saw since we built both dummy APIs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.414,
          "end": 12.96,
          "en": "there aren't too many differences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.96,
          "end": 15.88,
          "en": "but of course there are some small differences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.88,
          "end": 19.16,
          "en": "which of course can also be tricky to wrap your head around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.16,
          "end": 21.04,
          "en": "If you would compare the code though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.04,
          "end": 23.24,
          "en": "it's really not too different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.24,
          "end": 24.88,
          "en": "and that's a good thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.88,
          "end": 29.42,
          "en": "It means that switching from Node to Deno will be easy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.42,
          "end": 32.5,
          "en": "Of course, also the other way around though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.5,
          "end": 34.46,
          "en": "There are some core differences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.46,
          "end": 36.76,
          "en": "in the philosophies, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.76,
          "end": 39.1,
          "en": "The permission thing is an important difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.1,
          "end": 42.1,
          "en": "The fact that Deno embraces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.1,
          "end": 44.65,
          "en": "modern JavaScript and TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.65,
          "end": 47.21,
          "en": "out of the box so that you don't need to bring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.21,
          "end": 52.015,
          "en": "any extra tools or opt into extra experimental features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.015,
          "end": 55.52,
          "en": "that of course also can be very nice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.52,
          "end": 59,
          "en": "That being said though, Deno overall of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59,
          "end": 61.256,
          "en": "is still pretty new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.256,
          "end": 64.38,
          "en": "If we compare Deno to Node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.38,
          "end": 67.8,
          "en": "then we of course have all those different features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.8,
          "end": 71.41,
          "en": "We of course have the different philosophies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.41,
          "end": 73.68,
          "en": "also because Deno is simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.68,
          "end": 77.083,
          "en": "more modern than Node, it's way newer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.09,
          "end": 81.48,
          "en": "But we also have one other key difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.48,
          "end": 83.57,
          "en": "which is a disadvantage for Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.57,
          "end": 85.94,
          "en": "And that's the fact that it is very new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.94,
          "end": 88.1,
          "en": "Because of that, it can offer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.1,
          "end": 90.45,
          "en": "all those shiny new features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.45,
          "end": 92.94,
          "en": "It has all those cool features built in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.94,
          "end": 96.71000000000001,
          "en": "but of course it also means we have no big ecosystem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.71000000000001,
          "end": 99.35,
          "en": "that we certainly still have bugs in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.35,
          "end": 101,
          "en": "that we will see changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101,
          "end": 104.38,
          "en": "to some of the core libraries and modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.38,
          "end": 107.16,
          "en": "that we don't know which third-party modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.16,
          "end": 109.52000000000001,
          "en": "will survive and which ones won't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.52000000000001,
          "end": 112.94,
          "en": "And that overall, it's not really getting used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.94,
          "end": 117.719,
          "en": "by any production applications or bigger companies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.719,
          "end": 119.14,
          "en": "Node on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.14,
          "end": 122.59,
          "en": "certainly doesn't have all those shiny features built in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.59,
          "end": 124.41,
          "en": "and it has a different philosophy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.41,
          "end": 125.9,
          "en": "when it comes to permissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.9,
          "end": 128.47,
          "en": "and when it comes to the modules system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.47,
          "end": 131.23,
          "en": "where you have to install everything locally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.23,
          "end": 134.21,
          "en": "But for one, of course you might prefer that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.21,
          "end": 137.02,
          "en": "so that might not even be a disadvantage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.02,
          "end": 140.82,
          "en": "And in addition, even if you prefer Deno's approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.82,
          "end": 144.3,
          "en": "you still of course have the huge advantage for Node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.3,
          "end": 146.49,
          "en": "that it is mature and established,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.49,
          "end": 149.12,
          "en": "that we have no real major bugs in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 149.12,
          "end": 151.42000000000002,
          "en": "that it has a very strong ecosystem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.42000000000002,
          "end": 153.51,
          "en": "that it's actively maintained",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 153.51,
          "end": 155.47,
          "en": "by a lot of contributors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 155.47,
          "end": 159.11,
          "en": "that we have thousands of third-party packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.11,
          "end": 161.67000000000002,
          "en": "which we can use with Node that help you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 161.67000000000002,
          "end": 164.92000000000002,
          "en": "solve any problem you could face along the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 164.92000000000002,
          "end": 167.6,
          "en": "and that is of course getting used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 167.6,
          "end": 170.91,
          "en": "by thousands of companies and developers out there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 170.91,
          "end": 174.24,
          "en": "You not only find more resources on Node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 174.24,
          "end": 177.73,
          "en": "you'll also find more jobs and employers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 177.73,
          "end": 180.48,
          "en": "And personally, I think it's unlikely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.48,
          "end": 182.29,
          "en": "that a lot of companies will now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 182.29,
          "end": 184.92,
          "en": "start replacing Node with Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 184.92,
          "end": 187.03,
          "en": "Some might, but certainly not all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 187.03,
          "end": 189.83,
          "en": "and probably not right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 189.83,
          "end": 191.52,
          "en": "So, when it comes to deciding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 191.52,
          "end": 194.25,
          "en": "which one you should continue with,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 194.25,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "it comes down to which features matters to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 198.42000000000002,
          "en": "Which style do you prefer?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 198.42000000000002,
          "end": 200.65,
          "en": "Is that permission thing important to you?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 200.65,
          "end": 202.74,
          "en": "Do you like the URL imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 202.74,
          "end": 205.378,
          "en": "instead of local installations?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 205.378,
          "end": 209.034,
          "en": "Or do you maybe prefer Node's approach?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 209.034,
          "end": 211.76,
          "en": "But besides that, the maturity in the ecosystem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 211.76,
          "end": 213.14,
          "en": "should also matter to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 213.14,
          "end": 216.03,
          "en": "And there, as I said, Deno is very new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 216.03,
          "end": 218.86,
          "en": "and very immature so of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 218.86,
          "end": 222.21,
          "en": "here we have a lot of advantages on Node's side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222.21,
          "end": 224.26,
          "en": "So my recommendation would be that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 224.26,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "at the moment at least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 229.4,
          "en": "you look into Deno, you play around with it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.4,
          "end": 233.61,
          "en": "but you mainly use it for side and dummy projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 233.61,
          "end": 236.16,
          "en": "And it's really important to realize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 236.16,
          "end": 238.72,
          "en": "and keep in mind that Node is established",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 238.72,
          "end": 240.75,
          "en": "and it's not going to go anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 240.75,
          "end": 244.032,
          "en": "So even if Deno is going to become bigger,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 244.032,
          "end": 247.45,
          "en": "learning Node will never be wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 247.45,
          "end": 250.09,
          "en": "You would be able to switch to Deno easily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 250.09,
          "end": 253.22,
          "en": "so even if you need to do that, it won't be hard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 253.22,
          "end": 255.57,
          "en": "But chances are high that Node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 255.57,
          "end": 259.92,
          "en": "is not just not going anywhere today, but also tomorrow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 259.92,
          "end": 263.06,
          "en": "It's getting used by so many large companies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 263.06,
          "end": 266.12,
          "en": "It has this established ecosystem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 266.12,
          "end": 268.21,
          "en": "it has a proven track record.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 268.21,
          "end": 271.14,
          "en": "And the disadvantages of Node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 271.14,
          "end": 273.35,
          "en": "which are being fixed by Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 273.35,
          "end": 276.323,
          "en": "simply might not matter too much to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 276.323,
          "end": 278.21,
          "en": "So what you'll learn in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 278.21,
          "end": 280.37,
          "en": "is everything but obsolete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 280.37,
          "end": 282.24,
          "en": "It's completely up to date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 282.24,
          "end": 284.31,
          "en": "and more important than ever before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 284.31,
          "end": 288.209,
          "en": "Deno is a nice alternative which is worth exploring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 288.209,
          "end": 291.90999999999997,
          "en": "and hopefully this module got you started with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 291.90999999999997,
          "end": 294.36,
          "en": "but it's not like you should start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 294.36,
          "end": 297.93,
          "en": "replacing everything with Deno now immediately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 297.93,
          "end": 300.15,
          "en": "That is certainly not the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 300.15,
          "end": 302.713,
          "en": "and that might never be the case.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
